I’ve long thought there should be a required “Faraday mode” for smart appliances, making them operable to the level of their dumb forebears if the user asks for that, or if the vendor’s intelligent server goes down or is decommissioned.
Quoting @matthewsag
@smbrnsn The first thing I do with any appliance these days is disable as many supposedly smart features as I can. @googlenest is the world's most irritating thermostat. @Samsung's tv's are great, but they are also really annoying.

The expectation shouldn’t be there. Inundating arxiv with incremental work does not accelerate science and it annoys reviewers like myself. I always tell my junior colleagues: if you don’t feel that this will get you a best paper award, don’t submit.
Quoting @skoularidou
@NandoDF I do agree with this. On the other hand, the expected publications rate of junior researchers in ML/AI in order to get another research position is pretty much the definition of a sprint marathon...

